question:
A reader argues: "A text means whatever the reader takes it to mean. Since no two readers respond identically, there is no such thing as a wrong interpretation."

Write a response of about 350 words. You should:
- identify what is right in the argument;
- identify precisely where it goes too far;
- distinguish between an interpretation being different and an interpretation being unsupported;
- refer to at least one text you have studied.

